<http://data.silknow.org/object/1694cd1a-d1e7-3667-bfcf-f32a601c59fc>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A flat, square bag of linen embroidered in rococo stitch with red and green silk thread in a repeating pattern of stylized flower in a lozenge.  The bag is lined with pink silk and has a drawstring of green, pink and blue silk, silver thread loops and silk tassels."@en , "Embroidered linen bag, 1600s, British; silk thread, red flowers & green trellis"@en , "This bag dates from the mid-17th century and demonstrates a blend of old and new styles.  The flat, square format with silk drawstring is characteristic of bags from 1600 to about 1650.  However, the decoration reveals new fashions in embroidery.  The flat, even stitching and repeating pattern of a simplified flower in a lozenge are typical of embroidered purses of the period 1650-1700.   \n\nThe bag was probably intended to hold a keepsake, mirror, needlework tools or a gift of money, rather than everyday monetary use."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/def1334e-12d3-392f-9dba-62d2d74769df> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Embroidered linen bag, 1600s, British; silk thread, red flowers & green trellis"@en , "A flat, square bag of linen embroidered in rococo stitch with red and green silk thread in a repeating pattern of stylized flower in a lozenge.  The bag is lined with pink silk and has a drawstring of green, pink and blue silk, silver thread loops and silk tassels."@en , "This bag dates from the mid-17th century and demonstrates a blend of old and new styles.  The flat, square format with silk drawstring is characteristic of bags from 1600 to about 1650.  However, the decoration reveals new fashions in embroidery.  The flat, even stitching and repeating pattern of a simplified flower in a lozenge are typical of embroidered purses of the period 1650-1700.   \n\nThe bag was probably intended to hold a keepsake, mirror, needlework tools or a gift of money, rather than everyday monetary use."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/1694cd1a-d1e7-3667-bfcf-f32a601c59fc/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/1694cd1a-d1e7-3667-bfcf-f32a601c59fc/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.204-1928" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O158826> .

